I fixed #1221 and committed it with a full body. stream-json now handles SIGTERM, SIGHUP and SIGQUIT the way the text and json modes already do.

One thing works differently from the plan. The task said to end the stream with a final result event carrying "is_error": true, built with the existing builder for that event. No such builder or event exists: stream-json has no result event and no is_error field. A normal stream-json run ends on yoagent's own agentEnd, and yoagent sends one on cancellation too. So an interrupted run now ends on that same agentEnd, with its last assistant message at "stopReason": "aborted". I didn't hand-type a second JSON shape. The commit title still says "is_error result" because it's the wording I was given; the body corrects it at the top.

Before (current code, stall stub, --output-format stream-json -p ... -o out.txt): SIGTERM and SIGHUP killed the process outright. The stream stopped on a messageUpdate line, stderr said nothing, and nothing said out.txt wasn't written. Ctrl+C exited 130 but also left no closing event.

After (new build, timestamp printed with each run):

| signal | exit | stdout | out.txt | stderr |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| TERM | 143 | every line is complete JSON, last is agentEnd (aborted) | keep | (interrupted) + "was not written" note |
| HUP | 129 | same | keep | same |
| QUIT | 131 | same | keep | same |
| INT | 130 | same | keep | same |

How: a new Drain in src/prompt/sigterm.rs arms the existing signal handler for stream-json, but only on -p and piped runs; the interactive session keeps the default. On a signal or Ctrl+C it stops the agent, prints (interrupted) to stderr, and keeps emitting events until agentEnd arrives, waiting at most 2 seconds. main.rs didn't need changing because it already reads the interrupt for the exit code and the -o note. src/prompt.rs grew by one line, and its size limit in tests/module_size.rs went from 3992 to 3993.

Tests: three new tests in tests/output_failed_run.rs cover SIGTERM, SIGHUP and SIGINT. For the check that they catch the bug, I disabled the new arming line, confirmed the marker was there before running, and the SIGTERM and SIGHUP tests failed by name. The SIGINT test failed against the old code. After restoring the line, all three pass. fmt, clippy and the full test suite pass.

Not fixed, and noted in the docs and on #1221:
• When yoagent stops a run, its last message has empty text, so the partial reply only appears in the earlier messageUpdate lines.
• If a provider ignores cancellation for more than 2 seconds, yoyo stops waiting and the stream will lack agentEnd. I worked this out from the code and didn't test it.

I posted the before and after tables on #1221 as I took them. I also rewrote the two doc paragraphs that sent readers to #1221, since this push closes it.
